58,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think Candidate A sounds very kind. It helps with the status summaries and notes, so the people who are writing everything by hand might finally get some help and a chance to rest.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I must be cautious about Candidate D. My research showed that network coverage at customer plants is unreliable and device approvals are slow; a field app would be entirely dependent on those unstable conditions.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,George,,"I lean toward Candidate C. A central repository for supplier records addresses the data consistency issues Midori mentioned and, as a catalog, is more likely to be a fixed-fee implementation than a per-head license.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"@George, you're on a roll! Candidate C is exactly the kind of niche, practical tool that actually survives. It fixes the record-copying nightmare I found without demanding everyone's daily attention. It's a winner!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with George and May. Candidate C directly addresses the misrouted deliveries I found by fixing the conflicting address records. It solves a real, daily problem without requiring our overwhelmed developers to build something from scratch.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""George"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@George, @May, @Midori, it seems you all really like Candidate C. If it helps stop the mistakes and makes the work easier, then I think it is a very good choice too.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""George"",""May"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, it is heartening to see such consensus. Candidate C is a serene choice; it avoids the external chaos of customer sites and the stress of unreliable networks, providing a stable foundation for our records.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,George,,"It is a relief to see such agreement. Candidate C is the most fiscally responsible path, as it avoids the escalating costs of per-head licensing and fits within our current software allowance without risking next year's budget.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"Honestly, it's almost too easy! We've finally found something that isn't a vanity project. It's a simple, focused tool that actually solves a problem instead of creating new work for everyone. I'm all in for C!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Midori,,"I am very happy we have found a solution that everyone supports. Candidate C is the most balanced choice; it respects our budget, protects our developers' time, and most importantly, removes the daily friction our staff faces. I vote for C.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I will vote for Candidate C. It makes me happy to see everyone agreeing, and if it helps our friends stop making mistakes and feel less stressed, it is the best choice.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I also vote for Candidate C. It is the most stable option, removing the risk of external dependencies and ensuring a peaceful implementation for all involved.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,George,,I vote for Candidate C. It is the only proposal that aligns with our financial constraints and ensures we will not be blindsided by renewal costs in the next budget cycle.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"I'm voting for C! It's practical, it's focused, and it actually has a chance of surviving its first year. Let's go with the one that actually works!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Midori,,I concur. Candidate C is the most thoughtful choice for our team. It addresses the real-world errors on the floor while remaining sustainable for our budget and staff. I vote for C.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
